{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:InformationTheory.ComputationalHorizon","@type":"LeanModule","name":"InformationTheory.ComputationalHorizon","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity"],"declarations":53,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ComputationalHorizon.computationalHorizonStructure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ComputationalHorizon.computationalHorizonStructure","kind":"def","line":273,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-horizon.lean#L273-L284","doc":"The computational horizon as a HorizonStructure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ComputationalHorizon.HorizonStructure.horizon_nonempty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ComputationalHorizon.HorizonStructure.horizon_nonempty","kind":"theorem","line":262,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-horizon.lean#L262-L262","doc":"If degree-0 is blocked, the horizon is non-empty.\n\n**Parameterised 2026-09-14, and the defect here was WORSE than the\n`Prop`-universe one.**  This field read\n\n    horizon_nonempty : degree_zero_blocked → True\n\nwhich is a TAUTOLOGY: `fun _ => trivial` discharges `X → True` for\nevery `X`, so the field constrained nothing at all — and the\nconclusion the docstring names, *\"the horizon is non-empty\"*, was\nnever written down anywhere in the type.  The three conditions\nbeside it were `Prop`-universe fields, so an instance chose those\ntoo.\n\nAs parameters, all four propositions are fixed by whoever writes the\ntype and are visible in every consumer's signature, and the field now\ncarries the real implication rather than a vacuous one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ComputationalHorizon.HorizonStructure.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ComputationalHorizon.HorizonStructure.mk","kind":"ctor","line":243,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-horizon.lean#L243-L243","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ComputationalHorizon.HorizonStructure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ComputationalHorizon.HorizonStructure","kind":"structure","line":236,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-horizon.lean#L236-L262","doc":"The jet horizon blocks degree-0 data.\nThe computational horizon blocks degree-0 answers.\nBoth allow degree ≥ 1 data to leak through.\n\nThis structure captures both: given a graded algebra with\ndegree-0 vanishing and degree ≥ 1 leakage, the horizon\nis non-empty. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ComputationalHorizon.npWitness_poly_verifiable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ComputationalHorizon.npWitness_poly_verifiable","kind":"theorem","line":229,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-horizon.lean#L229-L232","doc":"The verification cost of an NP witness is polynomial (linear). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ComputationalHorizon.NPWitness.verification_cost_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ComputationalHorizon.NPWitness.verification_cost_eq","kind":"theorem","line":227,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-horizon.lean#L227-L227","doc":"The cost is exactly one step per crossing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ComputationalHorizon.NPWitness.verification_cost","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ComputationalHorizon.NPWitness.verification_cost","kind":"def","line":225,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-horizon.lean#L225-L225","doc":"Verification cost: exactly c steps (one per crossing). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ComputationalHorizon.NPWitness.witness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ComputationalHorizon.NPWitness.witness","kind":"def","line":223,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-horizon.lean#L223-L223","doc":"The resolution path (witness). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ComputationalHorizon.NPWitness.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ComputationalHorizon.NPWitness.mk","kind":"ctor","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-horizon.lean#L221-L221","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ComputationalHorizon.NPWitness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ComputationalHorizon.NPWitness","kind":"structure","line":220,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-horizon.lean#L220-L227","doc":"NP verification: a witness can be checked in linear time (c steps). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ComputationalHorizon.superPoly_not_inP","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ComputationalHorizon.superPoly_not_inP","kind":"theorem","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-horizon.lean#L207-L211","doc":"If a problem is super-polynomial, it is not in P. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ComputationalHorizon.inP_not_superPoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ComputationalHorizon.inP_not_superPoly","kind":"theorem","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-horizon.lean#L201-L205","doc":"If a problem is in P, it is not super-polynomial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ComputationalHorizon.superPolynomial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ComputationalHorizon.superPolynomial","kind":"def","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-horizon.lean#L196-L199","doc":"A decision problem has a non-empty computational horizon iff\nit is not in P (for any polynomial bound). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ComputationalHorizon.inClassP","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ComputationalHorizon.inClassP","kind":"def","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-horizon.lean#L191-L194","doc":"A decision problem is in P iff the computational horizon is empty\nfor some polynomial bound. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ComputationalHorizon.horizon_empty_iff_observable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ComputationalHorizon.horizon_empty_iff_observable","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-horizon.lean#L183-L189","doc":"The computational horizon is empty iff the polynomial observable\nsubcategory is non-empty: H_c = ∅ ⟺ R° ≠ ∅. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ComputationalHorizon.hasComputationalHorizon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ComputationalHorizon.hasComputationalHorizon","kind":"def","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-horizon.lean#L170-L181","doc":"The computational horizon: the tree has a horizon iff no\npolynomial-time degree-0 section is non-vanishing.\n\nH_c(L, q) = ∅  ⟺  polynomialObservable T pb\nH_c(L, q) ≠ ∅  ⟺  ¬ polynomialObservable T pb\n\nThis mirrors the jet horizon: H = V(h) where h is the ideal\nof degree-0 sections that vanish. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ComputationalHorizon.polynomialObservable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ComputationalHorizon.polynomialObservable","kind":"def","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-horizon.lean#L162-L166","doc":"The polynomial observable subcategory R°: the subcategory of\nthe resolution tree from which degree-0 sections are\npolynomial-time extractable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ComputationalHorizon.PolyExtractable.poly_depth","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ComputationalHorizon.PolyExtractable.poly_depth","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-horizon.lean#L160-L160","doc":"The extraction depth is polynomial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ComputationalHorizon.PolyExtractable.section_","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ComputationalHorizon.PolyExtractable.section_","kind":"def","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-horizon.lean#L158-L158","doc":"The degree-0 section. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ComputationalHorizon.PolyExtractable.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ComputationalHorizon.PolyExtractable.mk","kind":"ctor","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-horizon.lean#L156-L156","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ComputationalHorizon.PolyExtractable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ComputationalHorizon.PolyExtractable","kind":"structure","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-horizon.lean#L154-L160","doc":"A polynomial-time extractable degree-0 section: one whose\ndepth is bounded by poly(c). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ComputationalHorizon.PolyBound.depth","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ComputationalHorizon.PolyBound.depth","kind":"def","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-horizon.lean#L150-L152","doc":"The polynomial depth for a tree with c crossings. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ComputationalHorizon.PolyBound.exponent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ComputationalHorizon.PolyBound.exponent","kind":"def","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-horizon.lean#L146-L146","doc":"The polynomial exponent d (poly = c^d). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ComputationalHorizon.PolyBound.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ComputationalHorizon.PolyBound.mk","kind":"ctor","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-horizon.lean#L144-L144","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ComputationalHorizon.PolyBound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ComputationalHorizon.PolyBound","kind":"structure","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-horizon.lean#L143-L146","doc":"The polynomial depth bound for a resolution tree. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ComputationalHorizon.DegreeOneSection.path","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ComputationalHorizon.DegreeOneSection.path","kind":"def","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-horizon.lean#L138-L138","doc":"The resolution path: a choice at each crossing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ComputationalHorizon.DegreeOneSection.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ComputationalHorizon.DegreeOneSection.mk","kind":"ctor","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-horizon.lean#L136-L136","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ComputationalHorizon.DegreeOneSection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ComputationalHorizon.DegreeOneSection","kind":"structure","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-horizon.lean#L134-L138","doc":"A degree-≥1 section: a witness (resolution path) verifiable in\npoly(c) steps.  Linear transport through the tree. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ComputationalHorizon.DegreeZeroSection.vanishes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ComputationalHorizon.DegreeZeroSection.vanishes","kind":"def","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-horizon.lean#L130-L132","doc":"A degree-0 section vanishes if it returns 0 for all q. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ComputationalHorizon.DegreeZeroSection.extract","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ComputationalHorizon.DegreeZeroSection.extract","kind":"def","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-horizon.lean#L128-L128","doc":"The extraction function: given q, returns the extracted value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ComputationalHorizon.DegreeZeroSection.depth","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ComputationalHorizon.DegreeZeroSection.depth","kind":"def","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-horizon.lean#L126-L126","doc":"The extraction depth. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ComputationalHorizon.DegreeZeroSection.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ComputationalHorizon.DegreeZeroSection.mk","kind":"ctor","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-horizon.lean#L124-L124","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ComputationalHorizon.DegreeZeroSection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ComputationalHorizon.DegreeZeroSection","kind":"structure","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-horizon.lean#L121-L128","doc":"A degree-0 section on the resolution tree at depth k:\nan extraction of the Skein polynomial value from the partial\nresolution at depth k. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ComputationalHorizon.SkeinPolynomial.leafWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ComputationalHorizon.SkeinPolynomial.leafWeight","kind":"def","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-horizon.lean#L110-L110","doc":"Weight of each leaf at depth c. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ComputationalHorizon.SkeinPolynomial.tree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ComputationalHorizon.SkeinPolynomial.tree","kind":"def","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-horizon.lean#L108-L108","doc":"The resolution tree. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ComputationalHorizon.SkeinPolynomial.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ComputationalHorizon.SkeinPolynomial.mk","kind":"ctor","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-horizon.lean#L106-L106","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ComputationalHorizon.SkeinPolynomial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ComputationalHorizon.SkeinPolynomial","kind":"structure","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-horizon.lean#L105-L110","doc":"The Skein polynomial P_L(q): sum of all leaf weights. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ComputationalHorizon.SkeinWeight.weight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ComputationalHorizon.SkeinWeight.weight","kind":"def","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-horizon.lean#L103-L103","doc":"The weight as an element of R_q. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ComputationalHorizon.SkeinWeight.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ComputationalHorizon.SkeinWeight.mk","kind":"ctor","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-horizon.lean#L101-L101","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ComputationalHorizon.SkeinWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ComputationalHorizon.SkeinWeight","kind":"structure","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-horizon.lean#L99-L103","doc":"Skein weight: the weight of a resolution path in R_q.\nEach positive crossing contributes q, each negative q⁻¹. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ComputationalHorizon.ResolutionTree.leafCount_exponential","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ComputationalHorizon.ResolutionTree.leafCount_exponential","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-horizon.lean#L87-L92","doc":"The leaf count grows exponentially with crossings. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ComputationalHorizon.ResolutionTree.leafCount_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ComputationalHorizon.ResolutionTree.leafCount_pos","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-horizon.lean#L81-L85","doc":"The leaf count is always positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ComputationalHorizon.ResolutionTree.leafCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ComputationalHorizon.ResolutionTree.leafCount","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-horizon.lean#L77-L79","doc":"Number of leaves in a resolution tree: 3^c. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ComputationalHorizon.ResolutionTree.children","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ComputationalHorizon.ResolutionTree.children","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-horizon.lean#L74-L74","doc":"Branching: each node at depth k has 3 children at depth k+1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ComputationalHorizon.ResolutionTree.root_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ComputationalHorizon.ResolutionTree.root_unique","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-horizon.lean#L72-L72","doc":"The root (depth 0) has exactly one node. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ComputationalHorizon.ResolutionTree.nodes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ComputationalHorizon.ResolutionTree.nodes","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-horizon.lean#L70-L70","doc":"The type of nodes at depth k. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ComputationalHorizon.ResolutionTree.crossings_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ComputationalHorizon.ResolutionTree.crossings_pos","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-horizon.lean#L68-L68","doc":"Crossings must be positive for a nontrivial computation.\n(ℕ-positivity, not an archimedean/order-on-`R_q` condition.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ComputationalHorizon.ResolutionTree.crossings","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ComputationalHorizon.ResolutionTree.crossings","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-horizon.lean#L65-L65","doc":"Number of crossings in the link. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ComputationalHorizon.ResolutionTree.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ComputationalHorizon.ResolutionTree.mk","kind":"ctor","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-horizon.lean#L63-L63","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ComputationalHorizon.ResolutionTree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ComputationalHorizon.ResolutionTree","kind":"structure","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-horizon.lean#L61-L75","doc":"A resolution tree: the Skein decomposition of a link with c crossings.\nStratified by resolution depth k ∈ {0, ..., c}. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ComputationalHorizon.q_inv_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ComputationalHorizon.q_inv_param","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-horizon.lean#L50-L50","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ComputationalHorizon.q_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ComputationalHorizon.q_param","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-horizon.lean#L49-L49","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ComputationalHorizon.R_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ComputationalHorizon.R_q","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/computational-horizon.lean#L48-L48","signatureChunk":0}]}